{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1894"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c158): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c158.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1894"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge history/early-modern","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/history__early-modern.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",972],["+","The last great blank on the map lay in the far south, and it was filled by a Briton. On his second voyage (1772–1775) in the Resolution, James Cook crossed the Antarctic Circle on 17 January 1773, the first ship known to have done so, crossed it twice more and sailed right round the southern continent at high latitudes, the first circumnavigation of Antarctica. Pack ice kept him from ever sighting the mainland, and he concluded that any southern land lay beyond reach under the ice.\n\n"],["=",165],["+","\n| James Cook | Britain | first to circumnavigate Antarctica | 1772–1775 |"]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",930],["+","Der letzte große weiße Fleck auf der Karte lag im äußersten Süden, und ihn füllte ein Brite. Auf seiner zweiten Reise (1772–1775) mit der Resolution überquerte James Cook am 17. Januar 1773 als erster bekannter Seefahrer den südlichen Polarkreis, überquerte ihn noch zweimal und umsegelte den Südkontinent in hohen Breiten vollständig – die erste Umrundung der Antarktis. Das Packeis hinderte ihn daran, je das Festland zu sichten, und er schloss, dass jedes Südland unerreichbar unter dem Eis liege.\n\n"],["=",163],["+","\n| James Cook | Großbritannien | erste Umrundung der Antarktis | 1772–1775 |"]]}]},
